      "seq": 3,
      "text": "In the first minute after someone new enters a quiet Commons room, it's crucial to focus on making the first impression positive and welcoming. Begin by greeting others and introducing yourself to meet people and feel more at ease. Then, make yourself available to others, offering help or simply being open to being around. Set the tone by lighting up the area or ensuring everyone knows how to use the common spaces. Prepare to answer questions and offer assistance, allowing others to feel comfortable. Finally, relax and take a moment to relax before taking on more responsibilities.",
